cff-version: 1.2.0
title: SemiFab Constitution Corpus
message: >-
  If you use this corpus, please cite it and the Digital Judiciary programme
  papers it instantiates.
type: dataset
version: 2.4.0
license: CC-BY-4.0
license-url: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/
authors:
  - family-names: Kadambi
    given-names: Arun
  - family-names: Kuppuswamy
    given-names: Venkat
    affiliation: >-
      D'Amore-McKim School of Business, Northeastern University
abstract: >-
  An open 6,000-case conformance corpus for governing software change in
  semiconductor manufacturing operations monitoring and supply-chain
  control-tower software under a Digital Judiciary: a constitution of 103
  provisions (20 absolute) spanning export control, data sovereignty, SECS/GEM
  and equipment integrity, real-time latency, WIP and metrology immutability,
  recipe protection, software supply-chain provenance, AI-agent code
  governance, concurrency safety, cryptography, application security and
  CHIPS/NIST mapping; a contest-gated admission rule, a distinguishing gate, a
  lexicographic ordering over conflicting precedents, and a store of binding
  decision records with an enforced lifecycle. Ground truth is computed from an
  executed trace rather than authored. Ships a reference adjudication engine, 26
  conformance checks, a mutation matrix, and a cross-pack profile comparison
  against the VetPOC corpus.
keywords:
  - compliance
  - precedent
  - policy-as-code
  - semiconductor manufacturing
  - export control
  - software supply chain
  - AI governance
  - conformance testing
references:
  - type: article
    title: >-
      When Retrieval Binds: Appraisal, Authenticity and Disposition in
      Automated Compliance Decisions
    authors:
      - family-names: Kadambi
        given-names: Arun
      - family-names: Kuppuswamy
        given-names: Venkat
  - type: article
    title: >-
      Case-Base Formation for Precedential Constraint: Standing, Admission
      Rules, and the Reason Model
    authors:
      - family-names: Kadambi
        given-names: Arun
      - family-names: Kuppuswamy
        given-names: Venkat
